** Sorting Algorithms – Time & Space Complexity**

| Sorting Algorithm  | Best Time   | Average Time | Worst Time  | Space Complexity | Notes                                  |
| ------------------ | ----------- | ------------ | ----------- | ---------------- | -------------------------------------- |
| **Bubble Sort**    | O(n)        | O(n²)        | O(n²)       | O(1)             | Stable, simple, bad for large data     |
| **Selection Sort** | O(n²)       | O(n²)        | O(n²)       | O(1)             | Not stable, always quadratic           |
| **Insertion Sort** | O(n)        | O(n²)        | O(n²)       | O(1)             | Stable, good for nearly sorted data    |
| **Merge Sort**     | O(n log n)  | O(n log n)   | O(n log n)  | O(n)             | Stable, used in external sorting       |
| **Quick Sort**     | O(n log n)  | O(n log n)   | O(n²)       | O(log n)         | Very fast in practice, not stable      |
| **Heap Sort**      | O(n log n)  | O(n log n)   | O(n log n)  | O(1)             | Not stable, used for priority tasks    |
| **Counting Sort**  | O(n + k)    | O(n + k)     | O(n + k)    | O(k)             | Stable, only for integer ranges        |
| **Radix Sort**     | O(nk)       | O(nk)        | O(nk)       | O(n + k)         | Stable, often uses counting internally |
| **Bucket Sort**    | O(n + k)    | O(n + k)     | O(n²)       | O(n + k)         | Not always stable, depends on input    |
| **Shell Sort**     | O(n log n)  | O(n^(3/2))   | O(n²)       | O(1)             | Not stable, improved insertion sort    |
| **Tim Sort**       | O(n)        | O(n log n)   | O(n log n)  | O(n)             | Stable, used in Python & Java          |
| **Tree Sort**      | O(n log n)  | O(n log n)   | O(n²)       | O(n)             | Depends on BST balance                 |
| **Bitonic Sort**   | O(n log² n) | O(n log² n)  | O(n log² n) | O(log² n)        | Parallel sorting algorithm             |
